<Gooey xmlns="wonderforge.io/gooey/2026">
  <!-- Northwind's own toolbar, as a patch source.

       This exists so Cancel can put it back. A vendor's patch outlives
       the vendor — chromatica is a one-shot that exits the moment it has
       written its markup, so killing the process does nothing to the UI
       it left behind. Without this file, cancelling a subscription
       removes the billing and leaves the product on screen forever,
       which is a worse story than the one the demo is telling.

       Keep this identical to the Toolbar fragment in store.gooey. It is
       a second copy of four lines and the duplication is deliberate: the
       initial tree has to come from the page, and a patch source has to
       be a whole document. apps/introdeck/live.gooey makes the same
       trade for the same reason. -->
  <HStack Name="Toolbar" Gap="2">
    <Text Style="dim">{{.Wallet}}</Text>
    <Button Content="integrations" Click="{{.OpenStore}}"/>
  </HStack>
</Gooey>
